# Keep the Docker build context clean, deterministic, and free of secrets.
#
# SECURITY (this is the reason the file exists): backend/Dockerfile does
# `COPY . .` with a build context of ./backend. Without this file that copies
# backend/.env — the real production secrets file, which DEPLOYMENT.md tells the
# operator to create and edit directly on the droplet — into an image layer on
# every single build. Verified on production 2026-07-29: /app/.env existed
# inside the running bytescon_backend image, byte-for-byte identical to
# /opt/govcon/app/backend/.env.
#
# Nothing needs it there. docker-compose.prod.yml supplies runtime config via
# `env_file:` + `environment:`, so the copied .env was a pure stowaway: it
# granted no capability and leaked everything to anyone who could pull the
# image, `docker save` it, or read a layer.
#
# Excluding node_modules/dist also stops a host build from perturbing layer
# caching or shipping stale compiled output (the same reasoning as
# frontend/.dockerignore).
#
# Do NOT add prisma/, src/, tsconfig*.json or package*.json here — the image
# build runs `npx prisma generate` and `npm run build` and needs all of them.

# Secrets — never in an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.prod.example
!.env.test

# Rebuilt inside the image
node_modules
dist

# Host-only noise
.git
.gitignore
*.log
logs
coverage
.vscode
.idea
uploads
tmp
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.prod
.dockerignore
